---
// Fig. for "FFT and NTT": multiplying two polynomials is the same as
// multiplying their values at the same points — worked at the 4th roots
// of unity mod 13 (1, 5, 12, 8).
---
<svg viewBox="0 0 760 540" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;">
  <text x="380" y="26" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="16" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">values instead of coefficients</text>

  <rect x="40" y="46" width="680" height="42" rx="10" fill="#111c2e" stroke="#3ab7ff" stroke-width="1.5" />
  <text x="380" y="72" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="13.5" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">Is there an easier way to multiply polynomials?</text>

  <rect x="40" y="96" width="680" height="42" rx="10" fill="#111c2e" stroke="#3ab7ff" stroke-width="1.5" />
  <text x="380" y="122" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="13" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">multiplying two polynomials = multiplying their values at the same points</text>

  <text x="380" y="160" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="12.5" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">use the 4th roots of unity mod 13:</text>
  <text x="380" y="192" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="18" font-weight="800" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">1, 5, 12, 8</text>

  <text x="380" y="226" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="12" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">STEP 1 &#8212; values of f = 1 + 2x</text>
  <text x="380" y="250" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="12.5" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">f(1) = 3, f(5) = 1 + 10 = 11, f(12) = 1 + 24 = 25 = 12, f(8) = 1 + 16 = 17 = 4</text>

  <text x="380" y="282" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="12" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">STEP 2 &#8212; values of g = 3 + x</text>
  <text x="380" y="306" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="13.5" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">g(1) = 4, g(5) = 8, g(12) = 15 = 2, g(8) = 11</text>

  <text x="380" y="338" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="12" font-weight="700" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">STEP 3 &#8212; multiply point by point</text>
  <text x="380" y="362" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="13.5" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">3 &#215; 4 = 12, 11 &#215; 8 = 88 = 10, 12 &#215; 2 = 24 = 11, 4 &#215; 11 = 44 = 5</text>

  <rect x="200" y="384" width="360" height="42" rx="10" fill="#0e1f16" stroke="#5ddc8a" stroke-width="1.8" />
  <text x="380" y="410" text-anchor="middle" fill="#5ddc8a" font-size="14" font-weight="800" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">values of the answer: (12, 10, 11, 5)</text>

  <text x="380" y="450" text-anchor="middle" fill="#e9eef5" font-size="13" font-family="SF Mono, Fira Code, Consolas, monospace">3 + 7x + 2x<tspan dy="-6" font-size="65%">2</tspan><tspan dy="6"> at x = 5: 3 + 35 + 50 = 88 = 10 &#10003;</tspan></text>

  <line x1="40" y1="472" x2="720" y2="472" stroke="#223049" stroke-width="1" />
  <text x="380" y="496" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8fdcff" font-size="15.5" font-weight="800" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">MULTIPLYING VALUES IS ONE STEP PER POINT</text>
  <text x="380" y="518" text-anchor="middle" fill="#8b96a8" font-size="12.5" font-family="-apple-system,Arial,sans-serif">4 points need 4 multiplications, not a grid of pairs.</text>
</svg>
